# A drifter's `reach` has `mutate 100`: every child's gene moves one step up or
# down (a sixteenth of the range, at least 1), never out of its range.
# Selection does the rest: a drifter that looks less far counts fewer
# neighbours, so it keeps budding where one with a long `reach` stops. A line
# that starts at `reach` 9 is pulled down, and the world fills with
# short-sighted drifters.
rules ../../packs/genes
seed 3
size 128 128
terrain water_level 0 rock_on_soil 0 rock_on_water 0   # flat soil everywhere
start drifter at (62, 62) with (reach = 9)

run 5d
expect born drifter > 1000
expect avg reach of drifter < 5
expect min reach of drifter >= 1
expect max reach of drifter <= 10
